10. **Known limits (follow-ups, not in this PR's `app/` budget).** (a) The existing page route
    `rme.handwriting-pages.image` keeps its pinned out-of-scope answer, 403 (`RmeClinicalDocumentReadScopeTest`,
    `ClinicalEvidencePrivacyTest`); the routes this PR adds answer 404. (b) CLOSED by §9 (M3.3 PR7): the clinic
    oversight viewer and the cashier's clinical summary now label an amendment page and the oversight image route
    verifies it. (c) The RME print of a visit prints that visit's own sheet's
    pages (unchanged): a correction appended to a book held by an EARLIER sheet (R7-1) prints with that sheet.
    (d) A page written before rule 240 has no visit stamp (`authored_clinic_visit_id` null), so §8.3 reads its owner
    from `sealed_by_medical_record_id`. `MedicalRecordHandwritingRepository::sealBookPages()` stamps EVERY unsealed
    page of the patient's book at the first finalize after the migration, so a pre-rule page whose encounter was
    finalized before the migration (and so was never sealed) carries the sealed-by value of that later, unrelated
    sheet: that later visit can name it as the corrected page and the encounter that really wrote it cannot. The
    original page is never changed (§8.1), so the effect is a wrong pointer (`mengoreksi halaman buku RM N`) only,
    never a lost or altered page.

## 9. The amendment page in the oversight and cashier displays (M3.3 PR7)

1. **Oversight (security review M1).** `OversightClinicalRecordService::handwritingBook()` — the patient history and
   the visit detail of the read-only oversight module (Finance Klinik, Data Analyst) — carries `rme_amendment_id` and
   the §8.5 label on a page an approved amendment appended (the amendments read in one query,
   `RmeAmendmentRepositoryInterface::appliedCorrectionPageAmendments()`, applied ones only — the label reader's
   own filter, because a page row never links a pending, rejected or cancelled amendment in the first place: only
   `approve()` appends one, in the transaction that applies it, §8.4); the patient and visit pages render "Halaman
   buku RM N · <label>" (`data-amendment-page`), never an object key.
   `OversightClinicalRecordController::handwritingPageImage()` serves such a page only through
   `HandwritingPayloadGuard::storedPng()`: the verified bytes (`image/png`, `nosniff`, `private, no-store`, audited
   `NATIVE_FILE_STREAMED` as before), 404 when missing or tampered, 503 when the storage read fails (review L2); out of
   scope stays 404 and every other page streams exactly as before.
2. **Cashier (review L4).** The cashier's clinical summary (`rme/cashier/partials/clinical-summary.blade.php`) shows
   the label under the page, as §9.5 decides it for the cashier; the image link is the §8.5 verified route.
